    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0297" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Merrill.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1889</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and read with interest your
                    dispatch No. 257, of the 6th ultimo, touching the political situation at
                    Honolulu, growing out of the recent controversy between the King and his
                    cabinet.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
